# The project's standard for the form of its files (doc/FILE_FORM_STANDARD_v0_2.md): Git converts no line ending
# of this project's files, in either direction, on any PC. What is on disk is what is committed.
* -text
# The folder GAIS/ is another project's and is left exactly as it was. For everything under it this file says
# nothing about text, so Git does there what it did before (GAIS's own attribute files, and each PC's settings);
# and its batch files keep the one earlier line of this file that applied to them.
GAIS/** !text
GAIS/**/*.bat text eol=crlf
